recommendation:
Add strict access control so only the session validation contract itself (via the trusted execution path) can call `incrementUsageLimit`. The function should only be callable via the validated transaction flow, not directly. One approach:

modifier onlySelf() {
    require(msg.sender == address(this), 'Only callable via session execution');
    _;
}
function incrementUsageLimit(UsageLimit[] calldata limits) external onlySelf {
    ...
}

Alternatively, if direct calls must be allowed, add an upper-bound check: the new `usageAmount` must not exceed the maximum permitted by the session permissions. This requires passing or storing the session permissions' max limits on-chain.
